Feature: Order Cache Rebuild

  Background:
    Given the system is initialized with empty caches
    And the AMPS clients are configured for the following topics:
      | Topic              | Client               |
      | RECALL/TICKET      | recallTicketClient   |
      | RECALL/TO/OMS      | recallToOmsClient    |
      | OMS/TO/RECALL      | omsToRecallClient    |
    And the bookmark timestamps are configured as:
      | Topic              | Timestamp                   |
      | RECALL/TICKET      | 20250321T135819.46352672Z  |
      | OMS/TO/RECALL      | 20250321T135825.12345678Z  |

  Scenario: Successful cache rebuild from transaction logs during startup
    Given the transaction logs contain the following entries:
      | OrderId    | Source           | State          | Timestamp                  | RecallQty | FillQty | FillPrice | Ticker | Currency | Fund      | PositionType | RecallType    |
      | ORDER-123  | RECALL/TICKET    | New            | 20250321T120000.00000000Z | 1000      | 0       | 0.0       | AAPL   | USD      | TEST_FUND | Normal       | Standard      |
      | ORDER-123  | RECALL/TO/OMS    | PendingNew     | 20250321T120100.00000000Z | 1000      | 0       | 0.0       |        |          |           |              |               |
      | ORDER-123  | OMS/TO/RECALL    | New            | 20250321T120200.00000000Z | 1000      | 0       | 0.0       |        |          |           |              |               |
      | ORDER-123  | RECALL/TO/OMS    | PendingFill    | 20250321T120300.00000000Z | 1000      | 500     | 25.5      |        |          |           |              |               |
      | ORDER-123  | OMS/TO/RECALL    | PartiallyFilled| 20250321T120400.00000000Z | 1000      | 500     | 25.5      |        |          |           |              |               |
    When the system initializes and rebuilds the cache
    Then the cache should contain 1 orders
    And the order "ORDER-123" should be in state "PartiallyFilled"
    And the order "ORDER-123" should have the following attributes:
      | RecallQty | FillQty | FillPrice |
      | 1000      | 500     | 25.5      |
    And no recovery actions should be required

  Scenario: Cache rebuild with state discrepancy requiring republish
    Given the transaction logs contain the following entries:
      | OrderId    | Source           | State          | Timestamp                  | RecallQty | FillQty | FillPrice | Ticker | Currency | Fund      | PositionType | RecallType    |
      | ORDER-456  | RECALL/TICKET    | New            | 20250321T130000.00000000Z | 2000      | 0       | 0.0       | MSFT   | USD      | TECH_FUND | Normal       | Standard      |
      | ORDER-456  | RECALL/TO/OMS    | PendingNew     | 20250321T130100.00000000Z | 2000      | 0       | 0.0       |        |          |           |              |               |
      | ORDER-456  | OMS/TO/RECALL    | New            | 20250321T130200.00000000Z | 2000      | 0       | 0.0       |        |          |           |              |               |
      | ORDER-456  | RECALL/TO/OMS    | PendingFill    | 20250321T130300.00000000Z | 2000      | 1000    | 30.5      |        |          |           |              |               |
      | ORDER-456  | OMS/TO/RECALL    | PartiallyFilled| 20250321T130400.00000000Z | 2000      | 1000    | 30.5      |        |          |           |              |               |
      | ORDER-456  | RECALL/TICKET    | New            | 20250321T130500.00000000Z | 2000      | 0       | 0.0       | MSFT   | USD      | TECH_FUND | Normal       | Standard      |
    When the system initializes and rebuilds the cache
    Then the cache should contain 1 orders
    And the order "ORDER-456" should be in state "PartiallyFilled"
    And recovery action "REPUBLISH" should be triggered for order "ORDER-456"
    And a message should be published to "RECALL/TICKET" topic with current state "PartiallyFilled"

  Scenario: Cache rebuild with discarded transaction logs due to bookmark timestamps
    Given the transaction logs contain the following entries:
      | OrderId    | Source           | State          | Timestamp                  | RecallQty | FillQty | FillPrice | Ticker | Currency | Fund       | PositionType | RecallType    |
      | ORDER-789  | RECALL/TICKET    | New            | 20250321T125000.00000000Z | 3000      | 0       | 0.0       | AMZN   | USD      | GROWTH_FUND| Normal       | Standard      |
      | ORDER-789  | RECALL/TO/OMS    | PendingNew     | 20250321T125100.00000000Z | 3000      | 0       | 0.0       |        |          |            |              |               |
      | ORDER-789  | OMS/TO/RECALL    | New            | 20250321T125200.00000000Z | 3000      | 0       | 0.0       |        |          |            |              |               |
      | ORDER-789  | RECALL/TICKET    | Filled         | 20250321T140000.00000000Z | 3000      | 3000    | 40.5      | AMZN   | USD      | GROWTH_FUND| Normal       | Standard      |
      | ORDER-789  | OMS/TO/RECALL    | Filled         | 20250321T140100.00000000Z | 3000      | 3000    | 40.5      |        |          |            |              |               |
    When the system initializes and rebuilds the cache
    Then the cache should contain 1 orders
    And the order "ORDER-789" should be in state "New"
    And the order "ORDER-789" should have the following attributes:
      | RecallQty | FillQty | FillPrice |
      | 3000      | 0       | 0.0       |
    And recovery action "REBUILD" should be triggered for order "ORDER-789"

